config ANDROID_TAGLMK
	bool "Task-aware Android Guided Low Memory Killer (TAGLMK)"
	depends on ANDROID && MMU && SWAP
	help
	  TAGLMK is an independent, task-aware low-memory management driver for
	  Android.  Rather than only killing under pressure, it continuously
	  reclaims cold anonymous pages of background apps while free swap stays
	  above a configurable limit, and only begins killing once swap runs low.

	  Tasks are classified into CRITICAL, SYSTEM_APP, PINNED and APP phases.
	  Android system core processes are never killed.  App kills are biased
	  by cumulative CPU usage time so that lightly used apps are reclaimed
	  first and heavily used apps are preserved.  Packages may be pinned by
	  name to grant them materially longer survivability.

	  This is not simple_lmk and does not depend on it.  If unsure, say N.

config ANDROID_TAGLMK_ARM64_NEON
	bool "TAGLMK ARM64 NEON prediction accelerator"
	depends on ANDROID_TAGLMK && ARM64 && KERNEL_MODE_NEON
	default y
	help
	  Use an ARM64 NEON accelerator for TAGLMK's memory-cache-load and
	  burstiness prediction, computed in Q4.4 fixed point combined with an
	  integer/float (intfp) scalar factor.

	  When this option is disabled, or when NEON is unavailable at runtime,
	  TAGLMK falls back to an equivalent basic 32-bit integer/float
	  (intfp-32) implementation of the same algorithm.  The fallback yields
	  the same decisions; it is only slower.

	  If unsure, say Y.
